  "notes": "{賢|かしこ}い is an i-adjective meaning clever or wise, emphasizing practical wisdom and good judgment.\n\nFORMS:\n- Adverb: {賢|かしこ}く (wisely, cleverly)\n- Noun form: {賢|かしこ}さ (cleverness, wisdom)\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {賢|かしこ}い⟦{選択|せんたく}→選択：03306_sentaku⟧: wise choice\n- {賢|かしこ}い⟦{消費者|しょうひしゃ}→消費者：09866_shouhisha⟧: smart consumer\n- {賢|かしこ}く⟦{使|つか}う→使う：00473_tsukau⟧: to use wisely\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {賢|かしこ}い: wise, clever (practical wisdom)\n- ⟦{頭|あたま}がいい→頭がいい：20316_atamagaii⟧: smart, intelligent (general intelligence)\n- ⟦{利口|りこう}→利口：03801_rikou⟧: clever, smart (quick-witted)\n- ⟦{知的|ちてき}→知的：13700_chiteki⟧: intellectual (academic)\n\nUSAGE:\n{賢|かしこ}い can describe both people and animals. It often implies making good decisions rather than just being intelligent.",
